# Keep the build context small and the image clean.
#
# Everything here is either rebuilt inside the image, irrelevant to the server,
# or must never be baked into a shipped artefact (secrets, caches, other apps).

# Dependencies + build output — reinstalled/rebuilt in the image
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/distZ
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. Critical: env files must reach the container through Azure's secret
# store at runtime, never as a layer in a pushed image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Version control + editor
.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

# Other apps and scratch projects in this repo — not part of the Live Tutor image.
# svg-test-lab in particular is ~1.2GB; leaving it in the build context meant uploading it to
# Azure on every remote build, which stalled the build before it printed a single step.
virtual-campus
gemini-live-test-app
svg-test-lab
testfolder
# unity-campus-poc is a 4GB game-engine prototype (Library/, Temp/ and imported art assets).
# Nothing in it is served by the Live Tutor, and leaving it in the context makes every remote
# build spend minutes uploading it before the first step runs.
unity-campus-poc
# direct-booking-rental is a separate client project living in this repo (~786MB with its own
# node_modules and build output). It is not part of the tutor image and must not be uploaded.
direct-booking-rental
backend/packages/*/node_modules

# Large binary assets at the repo root (design mockups, architecture renders, planning docs).
# None are read at runtime; together they are ~12MB of pure upload cost.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.docx
*.pdf
*.svg
!frontend/web/public/**

# Local caches and generated artefacts
**/.vercel
**/coverage
**/manim-cache
**/lecture-cache
**/*.log
**/tmp
**/temp

# Docs and planning material
docs
*.md
!frontend/web/AGENTS.md
!frontend/web/CLAUDE.md

# Python bytecode
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
